{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf","id":424015,"title":"If you would done Vikings Werewolf...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-01T05:44:36-08:00","id":424015,"title":"If you would done Vikings Werewolf...","content":"Topic for wild speculations on Dark Era to come that we fought for in polls from the last month. As the name suggest, I ask how you would done this historical setting.<br /> <br /> Myself, I would start with stating that at least till contact with Roman civilization ( and by this with Roman-based Uratha ), there are not all the Forsaken or Pure Firstborns from Norman side. Norse have in their mythology Fenris-Ur, but their lack characters like Black Wolf or Death Wolf. Only 3-4 Firstborns would have cults in the Scandinavia on the beginning of Era.<br /> <br /> With more often journeys in the South territories ( Britain, Gaul and Rus ) and coming with contact of Romanized Uratha, Viking werewolves would soak their myths and believes, and with them new Firstborns Totems. They even would do their own Pangaea Myth, based on Norse mythlogy, looking for common characters with Roman Capitoline Wolf and Luna changed in to local Wolf Mother and Moon Father figures.<br /> <br /> Also, interesting would be if Viking Uratha would take part in pillaging of churches and why. In <b>Dark Ages: Apocalypse </b>for cWoD, Garou were fighting with the Church because of infestation of it with Wyrm. I suspect that Forsaken Uratha would take part in destroying christian temples and sacred sites if their Totems would be jealous of One God - if humans are worshiping Almighty, the could not produce the Essence co easily. Spirits long ago has acquired skill to use mortal &quot;pagans&quot; cults for their ends, but monotheism is alien idea and enemy to their plans - so they use Uratha claws to get rid of it.<br /> <br /> And here is mine idea for Norse Pangaea Myth variant...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/137256-alternative-werewolves-myths#post137256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Mother of Wolves</b><br /> In ancient times, that we all almost don't remember, gods and giants, spirit and flash, freely walk upon the young earth. In this still warm from creation land many beings could be gods of powerful spirit, giants of formidable flesh, or often even both. One of them was Mother of Wolves. She was able to give death and life, destruction and birth. She was mother to all wolves, but also guardian of secret ways to commune with spirits, to walk between land of mortals and land of gods. She stood on watch if both gods and humans respect they place in creation. And she deliver massage between them.<br /> <br /> As Mother of Wolves was truly beautiful, she was having cubs with all different suitors, and those children become Firstborns, like Fenris-Ur. But on long nights, she would see Mani, Father Moon, in his silver chariot running in the sky. He was once man, but gods put him in the sky, to light the night with his silver armor. Mother of Wolves desired him so much, by her wish she shed her skin, become human for a night, and walked to his chariot in the sky. After night of passion, she returned and born First Pack, blessed with gift of changing skin and they faces, as both they mother shed her fur and they father is changing each night his face.<br /> <br /> But this miracle night wasn't enough for Mother of Wolves. Even if she knew her love only once defied the rules, she wanted to return to Mani and to be with him forever. Gods made this exception only once, and she made a new race of beings from this union. Afraid what could they love made more to the balance of the world, spirits not allowed her to return to the sky, even for one more night with her lover.<br /> <br /> She raised First Pack, and they Father would watch over them in the nights. She teach them her duties and hunt with them on those that broke the rules of creation. But years passed, and Mother of Wolves was denied the warm embrace of Mani. She let her duties as guardian slip more and more, as she dreamed of unreachable union. Her heart was filled with rage and envy. Later she would be known as Angerboda - One Who Brings Grief \u2013 because of horrible things she would let go on the world, and what she herself done to others blinded by emotions. Mother of Wolves was threat to herself, creation and her own children.<br /> <br /> And so, on next the night, Father Moon told the werewolves that her rule must go to past. They knew now Angerboda wouldn't let her duty free until she dies. So First Pack needed do this for the best of whole creation. But some of werewolves were to afraid and run from responsibility. Rest of the pack made this necessary sin. In dying breath Mother of Wolves cursed her own children so the silver, moon metal, would burn them to the flesh. Even if he couldn't totally lift it, Father eased it by adding that only weapon made of it will hurt them, as he was also lord of silver. But Mani only lifted curse on those that listen him and done what had to be done. Gods were furious from what a werewolves done and are to this day. They cursed People so humans would be afraid of them. And so First Pack would be called De \u00d6vergivna, Forsaken, from now on. And traitors of First Pack would be known as De Rena, Pure, as they did not want to be burden with sin of killing Mother of Wolves.<br /> <br /> Father Moon understood he must help his children when they Mother was dead and world have turned from them. But he had duties that need to be done, each night, every night, till the end of times. So he send Hjukis - once children he stolen from Earth's years before and now spirits that were his loyal servants. They were tasked to guide the People and teach the ways of the Moon and to help them in their duties to watch over barrier between Flesh and Spirit. Each Hjuki teach about only part of Fathers lore, as only he himself know whole. Father would grant care of each one as spiritual guide to each next werewolf. And so Auspices come to being.<br /> <br /> But still De \u00d6vergivna were surrounded by the world that hated them. First Pack needed patrons with the gods. They hunt down and plead Firstborns, first children of Angerboda. Initially those powerful spirits were furious and wouldn't listen, blinded by the rage for killing they Mother. but De \u00d6vergivna hunt and run to them again, and again. Finally Firstborns understood they need to forgive they half-brothers and half-sisters, and guide them in the name of memory of they common Mother. And so the Tribes of the Moon come to being.<br /> <br /> But the sins can't be undone. Not all Firstborn forgive the Moon his action. Wolves crave for Mani's blood for what he talked in to First Pack and each day and night <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Hati Hr\u00f3\u00f0vitnisson, </span></span>Managarmr, the Moon Hound, is chasing Peoples Father on the sky, letting to shown only one Hujki's face at the time. He become patron of De Rena werewolves and together they hunt for Father Moon and his loyal People. There is gods prophecy that someday all Firstborns will return to Moon for blood of they mother, lead by Fenris. It will be time of Ragnar\u00f6k and the gods will pay for they inaction when Angerboda were being murdered.<br /> <br /> And so, to this day, De \u00d6vergivna hunts the nights to fulfill duties that Angerboda left. They are watched over by Mani and his Hjukis. They are guided by the Firstborns under they Tribes, so they could understand legacy from Mother of Wolves. Even if both Hjukis and Firstborns are not easy allies, they respect and fear one another. And to this day they all hate De Rena. Untill the time of Ragnar\u00f6k, may he never come.</div> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T06:49:34-08:00","id":424090,"title":"","content":"I dunno about the Romanization, considering that the Viking raids started some four hundred years after the collapse of the Western Roman Empire. Think about how much our cultural identities have changed since the 17th century.<br /> <br /> And regarding the cults of the Firstborn; who is to say that all transferred to mortals? Hati/M\u00e5ngarme is obviously Silver Wolf, it's a giant wolf, whose identity is built on hatred, and who is destined to eat the moon at Ragnar\u00f6k. Obvious really. Fenris-Ur is even more obviously the basis for the Fenris Wolf. My guess for that is that Blood Talons influenced mortal culture enough that this giant wolf was introduced, and this several hundred years before the time this story is set. Over time, Fenrir got conflated with the fear and hatred people had for wolves, and he got transformed into a villain figure in the mythos. Kinda like Loki did after the introduction of Christianity.<br /> <br /> And regarding the pillaging of churches... Churches are rich. You want riches. Their god doesn't judge you after death, so why should you fear it?<br /> <br /> A lot of this comes down to how much the mortal faith influenced the Uratha. Considering that the faith in the Alfar isn't that far from an animistic faith, and the Uratha have obvious proof of their existence (although slightly different from how people understand it, which is understandable), I think they are pretty close to the mainsteam faith, although, of course, with their own heresies regarding the first-born and the Moon (who, as you pointed out, is a male figure in old Norse culture, along with a female sun.)<br /> <br /> All in all, I think they don't universalize their own version of the faith, angering a god known as &quot;the Battle-wolf&quot;, or &quot;the Wolf-foe&quot; (that's old One-eye, by the way) is a pretty stupid thing to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T06:53:50-08:00","id":424093,"title":"","content":"If Hati is Silver Wolf, what would that make Skoll?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T07:04:23-08:00","id":424100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424093#post424093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Hati is Silver Wolf, what would that make Skoll?</div> </div> </div> </div>Good question, perhaps he has no parallel? He might've been a mythical creation added for symmetry, after some bleed-through from the Uratha, perhaps. I think we'll have to see how Helios is changed in second edition, and it's relationship with the wolves before we can say for sure.<br /> <br /> Oh, also, we need Ulfhednar: <a href=\"http://mythology.wikia.com/wiki/Ulfhednar\" target=\"_blank\">http://mythology.wikia.com/wiki/Ulfhednar</a><br /> That's (to me) obviously Uratha. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T07:10:32-08:00","id":424116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424090#post424090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno about the Romanization, considering that the Viking raids started some four hundred years after the collapse of the Western Roman Empire. Think about how much our cultural identities have changed since the 17th century.</div> </div> </div> </div>Norse are not known as very highly worshiping Lunar dieties - they are more Wolf-lovers. I think that Mani as Moon Father would later addition from the contacts with Romanized cultures - and their Uratha.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424090#post424090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And regarding the cults of the Firstborn; who is to say that all transferred to mortals? Hati/M\u00e5ngarme is obviously Silver Wolf, it's a giant wolf, whose identity is built on hatred, and who is destined to eat the moon at Ragnar\u00f6k.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is really good allegory for the Pure Tribes - werewolves that hunt Mani on the night sky. I done good Pure stuff even before reading the <b>Pure</b> book. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424090#post424090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Over time, Fenrir got conflated with the fear and hatred people had for wolves, and he got transformed into a villain figure in the mythos. Kinda like Loki did after the introduction of Christianity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did not Loki were villian god even before Christianization? He was god of mischief and traitor of Aesir, does he not?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424090#post424090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And regarding the pillaging of churches... Churches are rich. You want riches. Their god doesn't judge you after death, so why should you fear it?</div> </div> </div> </div>It does seem a bit hallow reason for the Uratha. Humans - yes, you want reaches and gold to survive a winter. But Uratha? They do things because of deeper meaning of things. I have a problem to concive a Forsaken Pack that goes to planning and say &quot;we must sack this monastyr for it has many reaches in it&quot;. I'm more easily could see that their Totem demands killing some monoteists of fear to their worshipers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424090#post424090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All in all, I think they don't universalize their own version of the faith, angering a god known as &quot;the Battle-wolf&quot;, or &quot;the Wolf-foe&quot; (that's old One-eye, by the way) is a pretty stupid thing to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was more in the way of making Angerboda the Mother of three-four Firstborns, with Fenris and Hati/M\u00e5ngarme as leaders of two sides. I still have a problem with rest of Forsaken and Pure Firstborns to be found in their mythlogy, at least as WtF is portraying them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T07:20:03-08:00","id":424128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424093#post424093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Hati is Silver Wolf, what would that make Skoll?</div> </div> </div> </div>Uratha fighting with Sol ( Helios female figure )? Maybe the Forsaken Firstborns themselves, as the Sol hate the race as the whole, especially for their siring with Mani?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-01-2015, 10:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T07:20:22-08:00","id":424129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424116#post424116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Norse are not known as very highly worshiping Lunar dieties - they are more Wolf-lovers. I think that Mani as Moon Father would later addition from the contacts with Romanized cultures - and their Uratha..</div> </div> </div> </div>Whereas I think the connection with their moon-parent is way older than Rome, and came with them from the beginning.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424116#post424116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is really good allegory for the Pure Tribes - werewolves that hunt Mani on the night sky. I done good Pure stuff even before reading the <b>Pure</b> book. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or that's at least in the stories the Pure tell each other, about what Silver Wolf does.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424116#post424116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did not Loki were villian god even before Christianization? He was god of mischief and traitor of Aesir, does he not?.</div> </div> </div> </div>Umm... It is complicated. He sure was mischievous and caused a lot of trouble, but his eventual betrayal was due him being destined to do so. Let me explain. The gods knew Loki was going to betray them, and lead their enemies during Ragnar\u00f6k, and so did Loki. When the signs of Ragnar\u00f6k got closer, Loki became more and more of a pain to deal with, because he didn't relish his fate. The other gods, on their hand, judged Loki harsher than they might have otherwise, and they chained him up in a cave, and had him tortured by the dripping of venom onto his face. This did nothing to increase Loki's disposition towards the other gods, and when Ragnar\u00f6k came, and Loki broke free, he happily led the giants in the assault on Asgard. All of this because they knew it was going to happen.<br /> <br /> Now, if we look at how many of the stories Loki was in, it is pretty obvious that he was well liked by the people, and his antics were a source of amusement and drama, so he sure was popular.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424116#post424116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does seem a bit hallow reason for the Uratha. Humans - yes, you want reaches and gold to survive a winter. But Uratha? They do things because of deeper meaning of things. I have a problem to concive a Forsaken Pack that goes to planning and say &quot;we must sack this monastyr for it has many reaches in it&quot;. I'm more easily could see that their Totem demands killing some monoteists of fear to their worshipers..</div> </div> </div> </div>The Uratha have an easier time to survive than normal humans, yeah... But what about their family members? Their friends? Not everything needs to be mysterious, after all. Besides, this is a show of strength, and the People are pretty fond of those.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424116#post424116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was more in the way of making Angerboda the Mother of three-four Firstborns, with Fenris and Hati/M\u00e5ngarme as leaders of two sides. I still have a problem with rest of Forsaken and Pure Firstborns to be found in their mythlogy, at least as WtF is portraying them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think we should create a version of the Werewolf myths, but with Norse trappings, that cheapens both the Old Faith and the Forsaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T07:44:26-08:00","id":424152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424129#post424129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whereas I think the connection with their moon-parent is way older than Rome, and came with them from the beginning.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a race - yes. But as a society - I would not be so sure.<br /> <br /> Let's assume the Moon come to werewolves from millenia, all around the world, telling the same stories. It would mean we would have more or less Pangeae-theme Uratha society everywhere. Changed would only human trappings, story would be all the same. No Lycon werewolves, no Apollo werewolves - only Wolf and Moon, everywere, as they are only true and sustained truths - they have their Firsborns and Lunes. Werewolf history is the same all around.<br /> <br /> Now, let's see alternatives - Moon is distant Shadow God. Uratha, instinctively, know they are under Wolf guidance - because the change shape in to one - but Moon is more esoteric one of the pair. They need the direct contact with Lunes. But what if this contact is lost? If local Uratha does not know Auspices and their Oaths of Moon? They are just wolf worshiping berserkers - they are dedicated to their wolves roots - but do not understand their spiritual ones.<br /> <br /> Or in the Egypt they <b>only</b> know Moon. Wolf spirits are distant then ( because people do not worship them enough ) and only Lunes are answering the preys. In Egypt, Wolf is not to be seen in years.<br /> <br /> In both cases I can easily see that when local Uratha society makes contact with other venerating second of the Sacred Parents, they &quot;borrow&quot; they iconography, and understand what their worship was lacking, summon Firstborns or Lunes they did not have before.<br /> <br /> Basiclly is question - is everywhere in the world Uratha creation the same, or does local worship have a matter in this? Is Uratha from Neolithic age worship both Wolf and Moon, everywhere in the world?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424129#post424129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, if we look at how many of the stories Loki was in, it is pretty obvious that he was well liked by the people, and his antics were a source of amusement and drama, so he sure was popular.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could be connected with Iron Masters Red Wolf?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424129#post424129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Uratha have an easier time to survive than normal humans, yeah... But what about their family members? Their friends? Not everything needs to be mysterious, after all. Besides, this is a show of strength, and the People are pretty fond of those.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can get human motives, but with regularity of raids, Pack need to decide if their target is to defend local or to conquare overseas territories.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424129#post424129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think we should create a version of the Werewolf myths, but with Norse trappings, that cheapens both the Old Faith and the Forsaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>What would you support? That everywhere in the world Uratha believes in Pangaea Myth. in almost the same way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T07:48:46-08:00","id":424156,"title":"","content":"If you guys want to dig deeper into connections like the role of the Moon, you should research Proto-Indo-European mythology. Indo-European religion as a whole is its descendant, and various themes and motifs are repeated everywhere throughout it. From India to Denmark, you can find all sorts of similarities in the old beliefs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T07:56:56-08:00","id":424163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424152#post424152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As a race - yes. But as a society - I would not be so sure.<br /> <br /> Let's assume the Moon come to werewolves from millenia, all around the world, telling the same stories. It would mean we would have more or less Pangeae-theme Uratha society everywhere. Changed would only human trappings, story would be all the same. No Lycon werewolves, no Apollo werewolves - only Wolf and Moon, everywere, as they are only true and sustained truths - they have their Firsborns and Lunes. Werewolf history is the same all around.<br /> <br /> Now, let's see alternatives - Moon is distant Shadow God. Uratha, instinctively, know they are under Wolf guidance - because the change shape in to one - but Moon is more esoteric one of the pair. They need the direct contact with Lunes. But what if this contact is lost? If local Uratha does not know Auspices and their Oaths of Moon? They are just wolf worshiping berserkers - they are dedicated to their wolves roots - but do not understand their spiritual ones.<br /> <br /> Or in the Egypt they <b>only</b> know Moon. Wolf spirits are distant then ( because people do not worship them enough ) and only Lunes are answering the preys. In Egypt, Wolf is not to be seen in years.<br /> <br /> In both cases I can easily see that when local Uratha society makes contact with other venerating second of the Sacred Parents, they &quot;borrow&quot; they iconography, and understand what their worship was lacking, summon Firstborns or Lunes they did not have before.<br /> <br /> Basiclly is question - is everywhere in the world Uratha creation the same, or does local worship have a matter in this? Is Uratha from Neolithic age worship both Wolf and Moon, everywhere in the world?</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course local worship matters, but if it is a faith there that the Spirit World, as seen by the Werewolves, doesn't invalidate, why should they not believe in that as well? Why does the werewolf world view have to replace the mortal faiths?<br /> <br /> Christianity kind of makes sense that it replaces, because that one is pretty strongly incompatible with how the Uratha see the world, but Shinto? No problems there. Hell, the Shadow CONFIRMS a lot about Shinto.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424152#post424152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could be connected with Iron Masters Red Wolf?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or perhaps it was a Changeling who went down in legend, and the stories turned him into a god. Or someone getting influenced by the Astral archetype of the Trickster and made Loki up out of whole cloth. Or it was just a really good mortal storyteller who based him off of a childhood friend of his, who always was up to no good, and those stories became popular...<br /> <br /> Not everything needs to be werewolf-based.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424152#post424152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can get human motives, but with regularity of raids, Pack need to decide if their target is to defend local or to conquare overseas territories.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Uratha weren't that common in the overseas raids, because that meant leaving the homelands undefended for months or years on end, and when they did, they did it to take new lands for themselves to settle in, just like the human Vikings did.<br /> And you mention the commonality of Viking raids, what was even more common than that were trade missions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424152#post424152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would you support? That everywhere in the world Uratha believes in Pangaea Myth. in almost the same way?</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said that. I just mean to say that they shouldn't change the local mythology to fit their world-view. After all, there is nothing in the Norse myths that exclude the idea of Pangaea and the stories about Father Wolf. They can fit it in there. Obviously, they'd use the name Mani instead of Luna, but the First Tongue name would be the same (although with Father, rather than Mother, of course).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T08:55:06-08:00","id":424197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424163#post424163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course local worship matters, but if it is a faith there that the Spirit World, as seen by the Werewolves, doesn't invalidate, why should they not believe in that as well? Why does the werewolf world view have to replace the mortal faiths?<br /> <br /> Christianity kind of makes sense that it replaces, because that one is pretty strongly incompatible with how the Uratha see the world, but Shinto? No problems there. Hell, the Shadow CONFIRMS a lot about Shinto.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's probably that English is my second language, but I do not get it. Could you elaborate on this, give some examples?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424163#post424163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or perhaps it was a Changeling who went down in legend, and the stories turned him into a god. Or someone getting influenced by the Astral archetype of the Trickster and made Loki up out of whole cloth. Or it was just a really good mortal storyteller who based him off of a childhood friend of his, who always was up to no good, and those stories became popular...<br /> <br /> Not everything needs to be werewolf-based.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I can clearly understand that. What I have in my mind was should not Uratha promote Red Wolf worship as Loki's? Both are tricksters, dedicated to mischive and Cunning (as Renown).<br /> <br /> I mean - you could not persuade humans to worship Red Wolf, patron of Wolfness Trickery. But you could make them believe in (Red) Loki, trickster assuming many forms. When Norman Iron Master is calling for help would he cry for Red Wolf or Loki ( assuming he thinks they are both the same being in his mind )?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424163#post424163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Uratha weren't that common in the overseas raids, because that meant leaving the homelands undefended for months or years on end, and when they did, they did it to take new lands for themselves to settle in, just like the human Vikings did.<br /> And you mention the commonality of Viking raids, what was even more common than that were trade missions.</div> </div> </div> </div>We will have Vikings Werewolf, not Norman. The raids ( or trade missions ) are the heart of the Era / at least as it sounds / so let's focus on why would Uratha go overseas, in whole Pack, with Wolf-Blooded and humans in them. I say that Totem being jealous of One God is probable scenario - beside &quot;more money, women and slaves&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424163#post424163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never said that. I just mean to say that they shouldn't change the local mythology to fit their world-view. After all, there is nothing in the Norse myths that exclude the idea of Pangaea and the stories about Father Wolf. They can fit it in there. Obviously, they'd use the name Mani instead of Luna, but the First Tongue name would be the same (although with Father, rather than Mother, of course).</div> </div> </div> </div>How many would be Pangaea part of local Uratha folklore, and how much Norse myths? Do we need all Firstborns as literal Wolf Gods? Or like Loki - character that could be antropohization of the Firstborn?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T09:11:16-08:00","id":424204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424197#post424197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's probably that English is my second language, but I do not get it. Could you elaborate on this, give some examples?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'll try, sure. But keep in mind that I'm just a hobbyist, and not in any way a professional when it comes to this, so what I say might (I say might, I think I have at least a basic grip on this) be just so much horse-shit.<br /> <br /> Anyhow. When we come down to the normal, people-level of the old Norse faiths, a lot of effort went into the appeasement of spirits that lived around the home or in the woods, or had special sacred places in the woods, these spirits (among with some other stuff, confusingly enough) were called Alfar - Elves. Remainders of this part of the faith held on for centuries after the Norse gods had been relegated to old tales, and it's fairly prevalent on Iceland even today.<br /> <br /> Shinto also talks about how everything has a kami inside of it, and that you should respect them, and there are also things about how old man-made objects also develop spirits after a time (I think the limit is 100 years). A werewolf who grew up in an animistic faith like this, wouldn't try to replace these beliefs with the ones the Tribes bring, but rather try to use them to compliment each other. After all, it makes sense that if the werewolf cultures were hidden from humans, why wouldn't their secret stories be hidden as well?<br /> <br /> The Abrahamithic faiths, however, are fairly absolute, and nothing in it includes the existence of spirit-like entities, so it's more likely that Uratha would cut completely with that kind of faith.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424197#post424197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I can clearly understand that. What I have in my mind was should not Uratha promote Red Wolf worship as Loki's? Both are tricksters, dedicated to mischive and Cunning (as Renown).<br /> <br /> I mean - you could not persuade humans to worship Red Wolf, patron of Wolfness Trickery. But you could make them believe in (Red) Loki, trickster assuming many forms. When Norman Iron Master is calling for help would he cry for Red Wolf or Loki ( assuming he thinks they are both the same being in his mind )?</div> </div> </div> </div>But Loki is the blood-brother of Odin. Would you really want to try to usurp his followers?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424197#post424197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We will have Vikings Werewolf, not Norman. The raids ( or trade missions ) are the heart of the Era / at least as it sounds / so let's focus on why would Uratha go overseas, in whole Pack, with Wolf-Blooded and humans in them. I say that Totem being jealous of One God is probable scenario - beside &quot;more money, women and slaves&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Normans weren't the only Norse settled elsewhere. All along the major rivers of Russia and Ukraine, the Irish coast, Iceland, Greenland, the Isles of the North Sea, the Channel Isles, the Dane-Law in England, Finland, the Baltic... And that's only where I know they estabilshed &quot;colonies&quot;. There were also Norse who settled among other people, most well known of these are the Varangians (which might be the East-faring version of the word Viking, by the way) of Constantinople.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424197#post424197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many would be Pangaea part of local Uratha folklore, and how much Norse myths? Do we need all Firstborns as literal Wolf Gods? Or like Loki - character that could be antropohization of the Firstborn?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the Firstborn necessarily need to &quot;be&quot; any character within the faith - Except in the case of Fenrir, obviously. And even from an Uratha perspective, he isn't the nicest of the Firstborn - It's not inconceivable that the Destroyer Wolf would be part of the world's destruction. The Pure, on their hand, might, or might not, conflate Hati with Silver Wolf, because of the similarity in ideas, but I wouldn't say it's neccessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T09:39:07-08:00","id":424237,"title":"","content":"Just a minor point to add to this discussion: In 2e, Luna is not presented with a definitive gender, I don't believe. They alternate pronouns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T09:43:11-08:00","id":424263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424204#post424204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll try, sure. But keep in mind that I'm just a hobbyist, and not in any way a professional when it comes to this, so what I say might (I say might, I think I have at least a basic grip on this) be just so much horse-shit.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's okay, I'm also only the &quot;fan of Vikings&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424204#post424204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyhow. When we come down to the normal, people-level of the old Norse faiths, a lot of effort went into the appeasement of spirits that lived around the home or in the woods, or had special sacred places in the woods, these spirits (among with some other stuff, confusingly enough) were called Alfar - Elves. Remainders of this part of the faith held on for centuries after the Norse gods had been relegated to old tales, and it's fairly prevalent on Iceland even today.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, prevalent &quot;household spirit&quot; worship. The same as with Romans, Greeks and many African tribes. It still does not answer if local gods should be introduced in to Uratha day-to-day folklore.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424204#post424204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A werewolf who grew up in an animistic faith like this, wouldn't try to replace these beliefs with the ones the Tribes bring, but rather try to use them to compliment each other. After all, it makes sense that if the werewolf cultures were hidden from humans, why wouldn't their secret stories be hidden as well?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because they work with their Pack. Let's say our Viking werewolf are on the raid with their war band Pack - 4 werewolves, 2 wolf-blooded, 8-9 humans. They gone in to heavy battle with enemy, are pin down. They are in the trap, lead by one of enemies soldiers. Is he more probable to curse the Loki, Master of Mischief, or to plead the Red Wolf, Firstborn of Trickery? Remember, less than half of war band can only know about werewolves. On the other hand, character from the animistic faith want's to call SOMEONE for the help in this kind situation. Would if be Loki or Red Wolf ( that should be a secret )?<br /> <br /> Also, thing with Fenris is odd one - if he is Firstborn, he's name should be secret, by your way of thinking. Why it is not?<br /> <br /> Maybe other question will answer ours - how the thing with Firstborn worship was solved in Mesopotamia setting? Did werewolves have their own secret pantheon, and did not called on local Wolf and Moon spirits? Did they not change the names of Firstborns for local pantheon representatives?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424204#post424204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Abrahamithic faiths, however, are fairly absolute, and nothing in it includes the existence of spirit-like entities, so it's more likely that Uratha would cut completely with that kind of faith.</div> </div> </div> </div>It maybe the reasons why the Totems of Packs are enraging the Uratha on raids and fighting with Church.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424204#post424204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Loki is the blood-brother of Odin. Would you really want to try to usurp his followers?<br /> <br /> I don't think the Firstborn necessarily need to &quot;be&quot; any character within the faith - Except in the case of Fenrir, obviously. And even from an Uratha perspective, he isn't the nicest of the Firstborn - It's not inconceivable that the Destroyer Wolf would be part of the world's destruction. The Pure, on their hand, might, or might not, conflate Hati with Silver Wolf, because of the similarity in ideas, but I wouldn't say it's neccessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not, but in the polytheism religions normal is reaction to call the patron dedicated to the portfolio. It's logical that Norse would curse Loki for the mischief and venerate Odin in battle. It's possible to put a bless to the Fenrir before the fight.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T09:52:54-08:00","id":424265,"title":"","content":"For those mentioning the Abrahamic faiths: Islam very readily adjusts to the Hisil. The Djinn are a thing in their worldview, and their place beneath Allah is clearly defined.<br /> <br /> Christianity and Judaism are the ones more likely to have ... difficulties. And Bale Hounds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T10:09:22-08:00","id":424273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424263#post424263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, prevalent &quot;household spirit&quot; worship. The same as with Romans, Greeks and many African tribes. It still does not answer if local gods should be introduced in to Uratha day-to-day folklore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but it's more than just the house-hold spirits. There's things like certain rocks you shouldn't sit on while waiting for game when you hunt, places where sacrifices to nature-spirits were held, and suchlike. It wasn't just the home, it was everywhere.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424263#post424263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because they work with their Pack. Let's say our Viking werewolf are on the raid with their war band Pack - 4 werewolves, 2 wolf-blooded, 8-9 humans. They gone in to heavy battle with enemy, are pin down. They are in the trap, lead by one of enemies soldiers. Is he more probable to curse the Loki, Master of Mischief, or to plead the Red Wolf, Firstborn of Trickery? Remember, less than half of war band can only know about werewolves. On the other hand, character from the animistic faith want's to call SOMEONE for the help in this kind situation. Would if be Loki or Red Wolf ( that should be a secret )?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok. Secret isn't perhaps the right word here, but it's insular. The nature of the Firstborn, and everything in Uratha culture is generally explained after the First Change, provided you didn't grow up in a pack that explained things (and that's probably rare). Hell, a Werewolf pack in 9th century Scandinavia needn't be that deviant in their rites and rituals, compared to their neighbours. They are a bit more accurate in their bl\u00f3ts to the Alfar, is all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424263#post424263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It maybe the reasons why the Totems of Packs are enraging the Uratha on raids and fighting with Church.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that conceptual war is too high and impersonal for totems on the pack level. More likely is that the werewolves have bound a wolf-spirit to them. And I'll explain what that has to do with things: Wolves in this era were seen as ravagers and destroyers, creatures of danger and destruction. Odin was a wolf-god, but all other mythical wolves were unambiguously bad. Wolves were bad news. Thus, a wolf-spirit in that era and place would've been a more destructive spirit than the more &quot;natural&quot; ones we see today, since humans devote less thought to wolves than they did then. Therefore, a pack with a wolf-spirit as totem would want to destroy things like churches, at least if they want to keep their totem happy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424263#post424263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, thing with Fenris is odd one - if he is Firstborn, he's name should be secret, by your way of thinking. Why it is not?<br /> <br /> Maybe other question will answer ours - how the thing with Firstborn worship was solved in Mesopotamia setting? Did werewolves have their own secret pantheon, and did not called on local Wolf and Moon spirits? Did they not change the names of Firstborns for local pantheon representatives?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fenrir is, indeed, the odd one here. The question is if it was the Uratha that introduced him, or if it was the people of Scandinavia who found him on their own. Considering their view on the danger of wolves, it's possible that the choir of wolves in Scandinavia was mostly dominated by Fenris-Ur's offspring, and shamans picked up on the great destroyer-wolf who was out there, and a giant danger to all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424263#post424263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not, but in the polytheism religions normal is reaction to call the patron dedicated to the portfolio. It's logical that Norse would curse Loki for the mischief and venerate Odin in battle. It's possible to put a bless to the Fenrir before the fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do NOT venerate Odin in battle. You did NOT want him to pay attention to you when you fought, if he did, misfortune might befall you when his Valkyries decide you should become an Einherjare right here and now. Gods to pray to in battle were for instance Thor, or Tyr, depending on if you wanted strength or bravery.<br /> Those who fought in the name of Odin were the berserkers, and other battle-mad people, and those bastards were <i>scary</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T10:11:35-08:00","id":424276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424265#post424265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For those mentioning the Abrahamic faiths: Islam very readily adjusts to the Hisil. The Djinn are a thing in their worldview, and their place beneath Allah is clearly defined.<br /> <br /> Christianity and Judaism are the ones more likely to have ... difficulties. And Bale Hounds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you are right. I forgot about that, thanks for reminding me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424237#post424237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a minor point to add to this discussion: In 2e, Luna is not presented with a definitive gender, I don't believe. They alternate pronouns.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. But Norse Uratha would probably give Luna one, since the Norse avatar of the moon was male.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T10:35:23-08:00","id":424293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424273#post424273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok. Secret isn't perhaps the right word here, but it's insular. The nature of the Firstborn, and everything in Uratha culture is generally explained after the First Change, provided you didn't grow up in a pack that explained things (and that's probably rare). Hell, a Werewolf pack in 9th century Scandinavia needn't be that deviant in their rites and rituals, compared to their neighbours. They are a bit more accurate in their bl\u00f3ts to the Alfar, is all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you give an example?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424273#post424273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that conceptual war is too high and impersonal for totems on the pack level. More likely is that the werewolves have bound a wolf-spirit to them. And I'll explain what that has to do with things: Wolves in this era were seen as ravagers and destroyers, creatures of danger and destruction. Odin was a wolf-god, but all other mythical wolves were unambiguously bad. Wolves were bad news. Thus, a wolf-spirit in that era and place would've been a more destructive spirit than the more &quot;natural&quot; ones we see today, since humans devote less thought to wolves than they did then. Therefore, a pack with a wolf-spirit as totem would want to destroy things like churches, at least if they want to keep their totem happy.</div> </div> </div> </div>This sound like all wolf-spirits of that Era would be Fenris-Ur's decedents. But he would not be only one Firstborn active in that time. I envision that not only Blood Talons packs would sail to the South...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424273#post424273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fenrir is, indeed, the odd one here. The question is if it was the Uratha that introduced him, or if it was the people of Scandinavia who found him on their own. Considering their view on the danger of wolves, it's possible that the choir of wolves in Scandinavia was mostly dominated by Fenris-Ur's offspring, and shamans picked up on the great destroyer-wolf who was out there, and a giant danger to all.</div> </div> </div> </div>You imply that Fenris-Ur shown itself with it's kind to the Norse centuries ago and they venerate him out of fear from that day? That each time parents told their children terrible story about Fenrir Destroyer, they would generate Essence and Fenris-Ur's decedents grow stronger in power, overwhelming other Firstborns? Even Winter Wolf, that should be so prevailing in the Scandinavia?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424273#post424273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do NOT venerate Odin in battle. You did NOT want him to pay attention to you when you fought, if he did, misfortune might befall you when his Valkyries decide you should become an Einherjare right here and now. Gods to pray to in battle were for instance Thor, or Tyr, depending on if you wanted strength or bravery.<br /> Those who fought in the name of Odin were the berserkers, and other battle-mad people, and those bastards were <i>scary</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do not want the attention of Fenris or Loki, but I could not see other way for Blood Talons and Iron Masters to engage in their Tribal Totem veneration than using local pantheon representatives in normal community.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-01-2015, 01:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T10:51:52-08:00","id":424307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424293#post424293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would you give an example?</div> </div> </div> </div>Of what? Alfbl\u00f3t? Well, I know of one, that only the women of the house-hold were allowed to visit, it involved the sacrifice of a stallion, and more precisely, it's penis. This would apparently have various benefits regarding fertility, for the entire house-hold. I don't think I need to paint a clearer picture than that, do I?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424293#post424293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This sound like all wolf-spirits of that Era would be Fenris-Ur's decedents. But he would not be only one Firstborn active in that time. I envision that not only Blood Talons packs would sail to the South...</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course I don't mean that, just that the Destroyer Wolf could hold greater sway over the wolf-spirits of this area than the other Firstborn. I could easily see Kamduis having lots of contacts with the ravens, who were venerated as creatures of both death and wisdom, for instance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424293#post424293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You imply that Fenris-Ur shown itself with it's kind to the Norse centuries ago and they venerate him out of fear from that day? That each time parents told their children terrible story about Fenrir Destroyer, they would generate Essence and Fenris-Ur's decedents grow stronger in power, overwhelming other Firstborns? Even Winter Wolf, that should be so prevailing in the Scandinavia?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I'm not saying that. I'm saying that perhaps most of the wolf-spirits of Scandinavia were under Fenris' command, and when mortal shamans tried to commune with wolf-spirits, perhaps to beseech them to keep away from the livestock, and found that they all answered to a great destroying wolf named Fenris.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424293#post424293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do not want the attention of Fenris or Loki, but I could not see other way for Blood Talons and Iron Masters to engage in their Tribal Totem veneration than using local pantheon representatives in normal community.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I don't know. Loki, for instance always kept his word (a common trait among Tricksters..), and while a bit of an ass, he was ever a stalwart companion to his brother and nephew.<br /> But no, no one venerated Fenris, at least not among humans, Fenris was a titanic monster who would devour the world. You didn't want that thing's attention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T12:00:50-08:00","id":424350,"title":"","content":"Just throwing some things into the mix here.<br /> <br /> Tribes of the Moon does state 'Tales of human trickster-gods from Enki to Coyote resonate with Sagrim-Ur and tie the Farsil Luhal closer to humanity. The totem\u2019s ties to human mythology aren\u2019t just nice touches; through Merits such as Synergistics, Iron Masters can twist human rituals to channel their own spirit magics.' While it doesn't mean Red Wolf is Loki, they could still have a connection with one another.<br /> <br /> In the core book the Lodge of Lightning is mentioned, they revere Red Wolf but take patronage from 'Lightning itself' which is called 'many different names by many different cultures - Ogun, Zeus, Raiden, Thor - but the Lightning dancers recognize it as the spirit of precision, inspiration and focused power.'<br /> <br /> Blasphemies also has the Choosers of the Slain mot, the Valkyrja, who explicitly seem to believe that Father Wolf and Odin are one in the same.<br /> <br /> Also for Skoll, while Seidmadr is right and not everything has to be werewolf, it is possible that, like Soulless Wolf may be the Ninth Firstborn, there may be others that are more concerned with other things than being a totem to the Forsaken or Pure, like chasing the sun. Though we should be getting more information on Helios and why it is upset with the Forsaken with the new book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-01-2015, 03:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T12:00:55-08:00","id":424351,"title":"","content":"Okay, maybe we return to the design principles for one. I was going for Tribal diversity, with connecting humans worship gods with Tribal Totems - in that way Bone Shadows in Scandinavia are different beings than Bone Shadows, let's say, in Spain. By my paradigm Loki could be &quot;common name&quot; for Red Wolf, used in public, in the Herd - as in Norse mythology we do not have suitable wolf god itself ( except Fenris ).<br /> <br /> You are saying that Tribal Totems should be once and in changeable. That Red Wolf in each &quot;barbaric&quot; culture should be worshiped as a Red Wolf. But then, we have a new Mother/Father Wolf and Moon/Luna paradigm in 2ed.<br /> <br /> I ask - if Uratha race parents spirits, that are higher in spiritual hierarchy, can be worshiped in more than one form - especially human one for the Moon - why cannot Firstborns be worshiped &quot;in open&quot; as closest human gods of region?<br /> <br /> I just have this weird feeling that Norse Uratha would easier say about Loki, than a Red Wolf in casual talk - just like Japanese one would call rather Amaterasu, but not Iduth by her name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-01-2015, 03:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T12:37:52-08:00","id":424368,"title":"","content":"That is one of the big bonuses of legends spread by word of mouth. They're more fluid and adaptable. You are more free to make them more relevant by attaching them to cultures and phenomenon. While I'm sure there would be packs that eschew their Norse myth altogether and go straight to calling them by their Firstborn names, there are others who see something in their totems and attach them to their own religious beliefs. With the idea that high-rank spirits like the Firstborn can create powerful avatars of lesser rank it's certainly believable that they could have created all the legends of gods, but that would be an ambitious and purposeless way to go about Werewolf.<br /> <br /> I like the idea that there would be some tribes that have no or little presence in certain areas, so I'd certainly go with that. But I don't know much about Viking religion besides the pop culture bits. Did they have religious wars? Was there forced conversion? The Pure Firstborn have an interesting place of being angry martyrs. Silver Wolf is in eternal torment, Rabid Wolf diseased and possibly Wound-tainted, and while less so Dire Wolf, it still hates that its Predator's Paradise was taken from it. So I've always attached them to the idea of more organized religion, so they would bebut that's just a personal bias.<br /> <br /> Also in terms of native fauna, were spiders common in the region?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T12:38:31-08:00","id":424370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424351#post424351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, maybe we return to the design principles for one. I was going for Tribal diversity, with connecting humans worship gods with Tribal Totems - in that way Bone Shadows in Scandinavia are different beings than Bone Shadows, let's say, in Spain. By my paradigm Loki could be &quot;common name&quot; for Red Wolf, used in public, in the Herd - as in Norse mythology we do not have suitable wolf god itself ( except Fenris ).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I see what you mean, but I disagree. I think a Bone Shadow from Svithjod would be different from a Bone Shadow from the Cordoba Caliphate, but that the main difference will be the human part, not the werewolf part. And I don't think a Scandinavian werewolf would like to insult Loki, or any of the other gods by using his or her name as a disguise for their wolf-gods.<br /> <br /> Also. Fenris isn't a god. Fenris is a monster. As far as we know there were no worship of it, no sacrifices held in it's name.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424351#post424351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are saying that Tribal Totems should be once and in changeable. That Red Wolf in each &quot;barbaric&quot; culture should be worshiped as a Red Wolf. But then, we have a new Mother/Father Wolf and Moon/Luna paradigm in 2ed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it is inherently Red Wolf, a clever creature whose avatar is often summoned to initiation rites into the Iron Masters. It is a spirit of innovation and curiosity, but first and foremost it's a wolf.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424351#post424351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I ask - if Uratha race parents spirits, that are higher in spiritual hierarchy, can be worshiped in more than one form - especially human one for the Moon - why cannot Firstborns be worshiped &quot;in open&quot; as closest human gods of region?</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you explain what you mean here? I don't completely get it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424351#post424351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just have this weird feeling that Norse Uratha would easier say about Loki, than a Red Wolf in casual talk - just like Japanese one would call rather Amaterasu, but not Iduth by her name.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I agree here. Loki is a fun guy, who is human at heart, whereas Red Wolf is a, well, you know, Wolf. And all Uratha Scholars know that Iduth is pretty damn mad. A lunatic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T12:46:45-08:00","id":424375,"title":"","content":"Ok, sorry for double-posting here, but it looks better than adding a titanic edit to my last post.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424368#post424368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is one of the big bonuses of legends spread by word of mouth. They're more fluid and adaptable. You are more free to make them more relevant by attaching them to cultures and phenomenon. While I'm sure there would be packs that eschew their Norse myth altogether and go straight to calling them by their Firstborn names, there are others who see something in their totems and attach them to their own religious beliefs. With the idea that high-rank spirits like the Firstborn can create powerful avatars of lesser rank it's certainly believable that they could have created all the legends of gods, but that would be an ambitious and purposeless way to go about Werewolf.<br /> <br /> I like the idea that there would be some tribes that have no or little presence in certain areas, so I'd certainly go with that. But I don't know much about Viking religion besides the pop culture bits. Did they have religious wars? Was there forced conversion? The Pure Firstborn have an interesting place of being angry martyrs. Silver Wolf is in eternal torment, Rabid Wolf diseased and possibly Wound-tainted, and while less so Dire Wolf, it still hates that its Predator's Paradise was taken from it. So I've always attached them to the idea of more organized religion, so they would bebut that's just a personal bias.<br /> <br /> Also in terms of native fauna, were spiders common in the region?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'd like the Uratha to add their totems (we need a better name for that, by the way...) to the mythology, rather than replace it. I don't see any reason for the gods to be displaced.<br /> <br /> The old Norse mainly had religious conflicts when the Christian missionaries tried to buck in. To give things EXTREMELY simplified, it can be summarised thusly: Denmark split into factions, the Christians and the followers of the Old Faith, and they did war upon each other. In what was going to become Sweden in a century or so, it was more &quot;do as you wish&quot; with different house-holds converting or not (in a lot of cases, they just added Jesus to the pantheon, and let everything be, to the great dismay of the missionaries). Finally Norway was extremely resistant to the conversion to Christianity, and the missionaries fought long and hard to get there.<br /> <br /> And yes, spiders are common here, but none are dangerous. Even the very worst aren't as bad as wasp stings. That said, during this time, it was warmer than it is now, and it's possible that more dangerous spiders from the continent could live up here. Overall though, spiders didn't loom very large in the mythology up here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T13:35:42-08:00","id":424431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424370#post424370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, I see what you mean, but I disagree. I think a Bone Shadow from Svithjod would be different from a Bone Shadow from the Cordoba Caliphate, but that the main difference will be the human part, not the werewolf part. And I don't think a Scandinavian werewolf would like to insult Loki, or any of the other gods by using his or her name as a disguise for their wolf-gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>And here I must disagree with you - one of major part of human half for werewolf is his human upbringing. If you are Christian going through Frist Change you will have very different take on <i>Hisil</i> than a Muslim. I envision that Norse Uratha that thinks about most spirits as Alfar and Incarna as eqal to \u00c6sir is different than one from Caliphate that takes them for Jinn, beings of Smokeless Fire.<br /> <br /> If Uratha of North would assume their \u00c6sir are real, leaving gods in Shadow, they could think that Firstborns are their more primal, bestial forms. If you believe that Angerboda is Mother of Wolves, your people myths have Loki, the Trickster that is also her son - and that Angerboda had Red Wolf, Trickster wolf son - you can assume that Loki = Red Wolf, don't you? Especially, for all the proposes, literal mortal gods cannot be found in Shadow as spirits - closest are spirits that looks a like some aspects of human gods. In that case I think that &quot;I'm using mortal god in place of our Wolf God&quot; is acceptable.<br /> <br /> But I see that in most myth Loki is lover of Angerboda, and Fenrir is their child. Still, humans could mess up their myths in here. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424370#post424370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also. Fenris isn't a god. Fenris is a monster. As far as we know there were no worship of it, no sacrifices held in it's name.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it would be odd for the Blood Talons berserkers to run with his name on lips to the battle. So what would they do then?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424370#post424370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, it is inherently Red Wolf, a clever creature whose avatar is often summoned to initiation rites into the Iron Masters. It is a spirit of innovation and curiosity, but first and foremost it's a wolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>What if it could not be only the wolf? What if his Royal Avatar be the curiosity-spirit - that looks a lot like some trickster god of local legends...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424370#post424370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you explain what you mean here? I don't completely get it.</div> </div> </div> </div>We agree that in Norse Iduth would be called as Mani, and in Rome Urfarah would be as <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Capitoline_Wolf\" target=\"_blank\">Lupa Capitolina</a>? <b>Tribes of Moon</b> or so point that Coyote is very close &quot;nickname&quot; for Red Wolf in their myths. If that is the case - why our Firstborns could not assume human guise in myths and become, for example, Loki if it goes for Sagrim-Ur? And other Firstborns could be connected with other local cults of \u00c6sir?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424370#post424370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I agree here. Loki is a fun guy, who is human at heart, whereas Red Wolf is a, well, you know, Wolf. And all Uratha Scholars know that Iduth is pretty damn mad. A lunatic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant that when two Uratha talk to each other, but are not sure if the other one is Uratha, they could use &quot;cypher&quot; and used Loki in conversation in place of Red Wolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T14:01:11-08:00","id":424478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424431#post424431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And here I must disagree with you - one of major part of human half for werewolf is his human upbringing. If you are Christian going through Frist Change you will have very different take on <i>Hisil</i> than a Muslim. I envision that Norse Uratha that thinks about most spirits as Alfar and Incarna as eqal to \u00c6sir is different than one from Caliphate that takes them for Jinn, beings of Smokeless Fire.<br /> <br /> If Uratha of North would assume their \u00c6sir are real, leaving gods in Shadow, they could think that Firstborns are their more primal, bestial forms. If you believe that Angerboda is Mother of Wolves, your people myths have Loki, the Trickster that is also her son - and that Angerboda had Red Wolf, Trickster wolf son - you can assume that Loki = Red Wolf, don't you? Especially, for all the proposes, literal mortal gods cannot be found in Shadow as spirits - closest are spirits that looks a like some aspects of human gods. In that case I think that &quot;I'm using mortal god in place of our Wolf God&quot; is acceptable.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why not assume that Loki = Loki, and Red Wolf = Red Wolf? Just because no Uratha have ever found their way to Asgard or Vanaheim it doesn't mean that the gods aren't real, just that they aren't here. Which is what the myths say anyway. And &quot;I'm using a mortal god in place of our Wolf God.&quot; is pretty offensive to the mortal god, so most wouldn't use that.<br /> <br /> And to be frank, the Incarnae are here, while the gods aren't, that means the gods are further away, and probably even more powerful. I mean, Sul and Mani (the sun and the moon) weren't exactly the top of the game among the gods.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424431#post424431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I see that in most myth Loki is lover of Angerboda, and Fenrir is their child. Still, humans could mess up their myths in here. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, although apparently in some myth fragments the various wolves of the myths have different familial relationships.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424431#post424431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it would be odd for the Blood Talons berserkers to run with his name on lips to the battle. So what would they do then?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we'd have Blood Talon Ulfhednar rather than berserkers. (Theme of wolves, rather than bears), but I don't see why not. Fenrir is a monster to the HUMANS, not the Uratha. They have a much closer relationship to the Destroyer. And I'll point out, that to the humans, Uratha are monsters too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424431#post424431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if it could not be only the wolf? What if his Royal Avatar be the curiosity-spirit - that looks a lot like some trickster god of local legends...</div> </div> </div> </div>Because a wolf is the core of what he is, just like the rest of the First Pack. Dire Wolf is a spirit of Wolf and Strength, Winter Wolf is a spirit of Wolf and Resilience, Death Wolf is Wolf and Death, et cetera. They are at their heart Wolf spirits. And they are all, according to the tales, descended from a spirit of Wolf and the Hunt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424431#post424431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We agree that in Norse Iduth would be called as Mani, and in Rome Urfarah would be as <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Capitoline_Wolf\" target=\"_blank\">Lupa Capitolina</a>? <b>Tribes of Moon</b> or so point that Coyote is very close &quot;nickname&quot; for Red Wolf in their myths. If that is the case - why our Firstborns could not assume human guise in myths and become, for example, Loki if it goes for Sagrim-Ur? And other Firstborns could be connected with other local cults of \u00c6sir?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would Red Wolf be Loki? There are no wolf elements at all with that guy. The only one among the Aesir I know with a wolf-theme is Odin himself. If ANY of the Aesir would be an Avatar of Red Wolf<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424431#post424431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant that when two Uratha talk to each other, but are not sure if the other one is Uratha, they could use &quot;cypher&quot; and used Loki in conversation in place of Red Wolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, a cypher is a good idea, but why use terms that could so easily be confused with someone else? And how would Uratha actually talk about Loki, if they used him as a code name for Sagrim?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T23:19:44-08:00","id":424911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424478#post424478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would Red Wolf be Loki? There are no wolf elements at all with that guy. The only one among the Aesir I know with a wolf-theme is Odin himself. If ANY of the Aesir would be an Avatar of Red Wolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wolf part is hidden in the context. We mark the Rew Wolfs cunning and trickery by pointing on great Trickster of Norse, the Loki character. Like Native Americans can point to him by mentioning the Coyote. Or Uratha are poinfint the Iduth by mentioning Mani on the North.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424478#post424478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, a cypher is a good idea, but why use terms that could so easily be confused with someone else? And how would Uratha actually talk about Loki, if they used him as a code name for Sagrim?</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought on this more and I got this idea - use closes god's to Firstborn portfolio and add his nickname. So Red Loki would be code for Red Wolf and Odin Destroyer for the Fenris'Ur. Things like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T04:16:30-08:00","id":425002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424911#post424911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wolf part is hidden in the context. We mark the Rew Wolfs cunning and trickery by pointing on great Trickster of Norse, the Loki character. Like Native Americans can point to him by mentioning the Coyote. Or Uratha are poinfint the Iduth by mentioning Mani on the North.</div> </div> </div> </div>Coyote is pretty wolf-like, and Mani is a moon-deity, so it's obvious they are related. There are, however, no wolf-like attributes added to any of the other gods, except Odin.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424911#post424911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought on this more and I got this idea - use closes god's to Firstborn portfolio and add his nickname. So Red Loki would be code for Red Wolf and Odin Destroyer for the Fenris'Ur. Things like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>But why link them to the gods at all? The Norse had a ton of Kennings, that is, poetical nicknames, for basically anything, they'd most likely invent new names for the First Pack. Also, they didn't mention Odin by name, it got his attention, and you only wanted that if you were dying anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T06:02:29-08:00","id":425081,"title":"","content":"I think Wyrd is discussing from a meta-perspective, whilst Seidmadr is arguing from a more in game angle; and that is the root cause of the disagreement.<br /> <br /> In my opinion, the wolf portion (that is their instincts, stories and totems) of an Uratha would be incredibly similar to every other Uratha. They'd know Red Wolf as Le Loup Rouge in France and El Lobo Rojo in Spanish (Sorry for foreign grammar mistakes!), but no matter what it would always be the same Red Wolf. Your human religion may lead you to call Red Wolf a jinn, a spirit, a demon or a god, but Red Wolf will always be Red Wolf. These spirits do not bow to mortal perspectives, they are exactly what they are.<br /> <br /> However, just because you've become something more than human does not mean you'd throw your old religious beliefs away. If it is a bad idea to invoke a deity, you wouldn't tie Red Wolf to that deity's name. Local variation is the cornerstone of Pagan faith, and few old religions had solid, unchanging pantheons. It would be easy to add Red Wolf as a local deity, which has been lost over time (or purged by zealotry). There is no need to over-write the deep, conflicted nature of the Norse Pantheon with wolf iconography and Uratha symbolism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T06:17:14-08:00","id":425096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=425081#post425081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Wyrd is discussing from a meta-perspective, whilst Seidmadr is arguing from a more in game angle; and that is the root cause of the disagreement.<br /> <br /> In my opinion, the wolf portion (that is their instincts, stories and totems) of an Uratha would be incredibly similar to every other Uratha. They'd know Red Wolf as Le Loup Rouge in France and El Lobo Rojo in Spanish (Sorry for foreign grammar mistakes!), but no matter what it would always be the same Red Wolf. Your human religion may lead you to call Red Wolf a jinn, a spirit, a demon or a god, but Red Wolf will always be Red Wolf. These spirits do not bow to mortal perspectives, they are exactly what they are.<br /> <br /> However, just because you've become something more than human does not mean you'd throw your old religious beliefs away. If it is a bad idea to invoke a deity, you wouldn't tie Red Wolf to that deity's name. Local variation is the cornerstone of Pagan faith, and few old religions had solid, unchanging pantheons. It would be easy to add Red Wolf as a local deity, which has been lost over time (or purged by zealotry). There is no need to over-write the deep, conflicted nature of the Norse Pantheon with wolf iconography and Uratha symbolism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you hit straight on the head with what I tried to say, only did it way better than I could. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> There'll be some inclusion of the Uratha terms, since obviously Mani = Luna, and Fenrir = Fenris-Ur (And probably Hati = Silver Wolf, at least for some packs)<br /> <br /> And it's not like mystery cults are an uncommon thing, where people have to be induced into the inner circle before they are told everything the faith entails. Mage does this to extremes, but the tribal myths also have an element of this. Non-Uratha simply aren't told about the myths, and the world from a Werewolf perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T07:03:14-08:00","id":425141,"title":"","content":"Has anyone dissected the Firstborn as concepts? <br /> <br /> Pretty much everything in the Shadow is a reflection of something in the real world. But the Firstborn don't seem to have a material world analogue and still manage to be, comparatively, immensely powerful. Is it just due to the werewolf population swearing to them and offering essence in doing the work of the tribes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T07:06:33-08:00","id":425151,"title":"","content":"I think they do have a material world analogue: Wolves.<br /> The #1 Wolf Spirit has been dead for ages, and no new one has taken his place. Thus, all the Essence that would've gone to Father Wolf stays one tier down, so to speak.<br /> <br /> Then, I don't think it hurts to have the Uratha around to do rituals to honour their totems and so on.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T10:13:15-08:00","id":425379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=425002#post425002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Coyote is pretty wolf-like, and Mani is a moon-deity, so it's obvious they are related. There are, however, no wolf-like attributes added to any of the other gods, except Odin.</div> </div> </div> </div>In pevious idea, whan I started to use nicknames of gods, I was going the Odin for Bone Shadows Death Wolf - but then I understand it would be something like \u201cOdin of Dead\u201d. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=425002#post425002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But why link them to the gods at all? The Norse had a ton of Kennings, that is, poetical nicknames, for basically anything, they'd most likely invent new names for the First Pack. Also, they didn't mention Odin by name, it got his attention, and you only wanted that if you were dying anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I want to see how you use Kennings in place of Firstborn in times of raid with fall of your war band being from Herd.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=425081#post425081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my opinion, the wolf portion (that is their instincts, stories and totems) of an Uratha would be incredibly similar to every other Uratha. They'd know Red Wolf as Le Loup Rouge in France and El Lobo Rojo in Spanish (Sorry for foreign grammar mistakes!), but no matter what it would always be the same Red Wolf. Your human religion may lead you to call Red Wolf a jinn, a spirit, a demon or a god, but Red Wolf will always be Red Wolf. These spirits do not bow to mortal perspectives, they are exactly what they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only in tales of Uratha they are putted in mortal population perspective. From the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/choose-your-ground/\" target=\"_blank\">official Hunting Grounds of Australia preview</a> we have this tale...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hunting Grounds preview</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This story is true.<br /> The Dreaming was a nightmare. The greatest Incarnae birthed everything from their blood, bone and flesh, but have you ever seen a birth? No one\u2019s having fun, least of all mum, dad and bub. <br /> Altjira gave us the land with water to drink and air to breathe. The Numakulla spread animals and plants across the world and Mangar-kunjer-kunja made people from the animals.<br /> Like all births more arrived than just the baby. Lesser spirits spewed forth to feast on this new world and preyed on the living. The Numakulla saw this and were angry. The flesh world was not for spirits. Any spirit destined to become flesh would be born into the world through flesh. <br /> The spirits cried, begged and fought but did not have the strength to defy.<br /> The Numukalla asked Altjira to make a Yenpe to divide the worlds of spirit and flesh, so he did. <br /> The Numukalla told Mother Luna and Father Wolf to protect this skin. Mother Luna guided Father Wolf as he hunted but both knew he needed help. He needed children with gifts of wolf and moon, so Mother and Father mated. Wolf birthed female Ingwarelhe and Moon birthed male Ingwartwe. They came together as the People, spirits born into flesh as the Numakulla said, made to watch over both sides of the Yenpe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Australian Uratha are using common werewolf characters, but they are totally put them in local population ( aboriginal ) mythology. Norse people toll themselves stories about Aesir and Wans, not about the monsterous wolves. How can you reflect Firstborns as part of Aesir Sagas?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=425081#post425081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, just because you've become something more than human does not mean you'd throw your old religious beliefs away. If it is a bad idea to invoke a deity, you wouldn't tie Red Wolf to that deity's name. Local variation is the cornerstone of Pagan faith, and few old religions had solid, unchanging pantheons. It would be easy to add Red Wolf as a local deity, which has been lost over time (or purged by zealotry). There is no need to over-write the deep, conflicted nature of the Norse Pantheon with wolf iconography and Uratha symbolism.</div> </div> </div> </div>In game reality - yes, it is. We have our war band Pack, lead by PCs Uratha. Blood Talon players, that have a \u00dalfhe\u00f0inn character, want to summon the Fenris\u2019Ur Rage in coming battle. What character he can call - Fenrir, Odin or other? Rember, he is surrounded by the Herd part of his Pack - but also would want the blessing of Rage. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=425096#post425096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There'll be some inclusion of the Uratha terms, since obviously Mani = Luna, and Fenrir = Fenris-Ur (And probably Hati = Silver Wolf, at least for some packs)</div> </div> </div> </div>We need a lot more, as I point above. At least somehow integration of all ( used) Firstborns with Norse Mythology.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=425096#post425096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And it's not like mystery cults are an uncommon thing, where people have to be induced into the inner circle before they are told everything the faith entails. Mage does this to extremes, but the tribal myths also have an element of this. Non-Uratha simply aren't told about the myths, and the world from a Werewolf perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can understand this - but I imagine one of idea for this kind of setting are less restriction on to what you can say to your Pack, and it\u2019s distant parts.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s also good question for the 2ed Pack treatment in general - how much of Pack mythos human Herd parts of Pack know on the day-to-day basis, even in modern setting? Does Bone Shadows skulls-and-bones-style cult knows about Death Wolf? Iron Masters gang knows about Red Wolf? General Packs members about Firstborns?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T13:10:00-08:00","id":425593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=425379#post425379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In pevious idea, whan I started to use nicknames of gods, I was going the Odin for Bone Shadows Death Wolf - but then I understand it would be something like \u201cOdin of Dead\u201d. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Odin is a god of War, Death, Wisdom, Magic, and a whole bunch of other things. If he is linked to any one of the first-born, then it's Kamduis-Ur.<br /> Then again, Freyja is also a deity of War, Death, Wisdom and Magic... As well as Fertility and a few other exciting things. They are pretty broad?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=425379#post425379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I want to see how you use Kennings in place of Firstborn in times of raid with fall of your war band being from Herd.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, considering how obscure they can be, I don't think anyone would think you were talking about Sagrim-Ur if you called him something along the lines of &quot;thinker's friend&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=425379#post425379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only in tales of Uratha they are putted in mortal population perspective. From the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/choose-your-ground/\" target=\"_blank\">official Hunting Grounds of Australia preview</a> we have this tale...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Australian Uratha are using common werewolf characters, but they are totally put them in local population ( aboriginal ) mythology. Norse people toll themselves stories about Aesir and Wans, not about the monsterous wolves. How can you reflect Firstborns as part of Aesir Sagas?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think we have to. The stories are rich enough without them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=425379#post425379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In game reality - yes, it is. We have our war band Pack, lead by PCs Uratha. Blood Talon players, that have a \u00dalfhe\u00f0inn character, want to summon the Fenris\u2019Ur Rage in coming battle. What character he can call - Fenrir, Odin or other? Rember, he is surrounded by the Herd part of his Pack - but also would want the blessing of Rage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hungerer? Destroyer? Vargr? Chained one? Blood-soaked one? Third child of the hunter?<br /> Chained one is a bit dubious, people might figure out it's Fenrir, and third child of the hunter is just me assuming Fenris-Ur is #3, if he isn't, apply the proper number. It's not that hard, and the gods aren't needed.<br /> All in all though, I think you can say whatever you want, others are going to steer clear of an Ulfhedin getting ready to fight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=425379#post425379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We need a lot more, as I point above. At least somehow integration of all ( used) Firstborns with Norse Mythology.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I don't think we do. We use the ones who are already in there, but why should the others barge in and take more space?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=425379#post425379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can understand this - but I imagine one of idea for this kind of setting are less restriction on to what you can say to your Pack, and it\u2019s distant parts.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s also good question for the 2ed Pack treatment in general - how much of Pack mythos human Herd parts of Pack know on the day-to-day basis, even in modern setting? Does Bone Shadows skulls-and-bones-style cult knows about Death Wolf? Iron Masters gang knows about Red Wolf? General Packs members about Firstborns?</div> </div> </div> </div>Think it varies from Pack to Pack, in what they define as the herd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T21:50:31-08:00","id":426165,"title":"","content":"One of main charms of <b>Werewolf</b> game, to me, is mixing local human culture with Uratha - without them, game loose many in my eyes. Saying do not need to mix Norse mythology with stories of Firstborns is great blow to my game experience - I count that developers in final chapter will try at least this.<br /> <br /> Looking more in to topic, we can not use Norse gods as other name for Firsborns - but still, some patrons worship is natural for Tribes members. Here are mine propositions what would be main patrons for Forsaken Tribes. There are not spiritual beings, only that most members would worship them most in day to day lives, as being part of their Norse culture.<br /> <br /> <b>Blood Talons</b> - Odin <br /> <b>Bone Shadows</b> - Odin, Freyja<br /> <b>Hunters in Darkness</b> - Here is big problem, maybe they do not exist in Norse Tribes?<br /> <b>Iron Masters</b> - Loki<br /> <b>Winter Wolf </b>- Thor<br /> <br /> Probably could be added at least one more to them in each - if you have ideas, write. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, I thought more about reasons for Uratha to raid churches in general - what about that their are looking for something? Like in local werewolves variant of Ragnarok there is Idigam that looks a lot like symbols used by Christianity and People want to stop them, partaking in raids?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T04:23:14-08:00","id":426423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=426165#post426165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Hunters in Darkness</b> - Here is big problem, maybe they do not exist in Norse Tribes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would they not exist in the Scandinavian region?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T04:32:30-08:00","id":426433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=426423#post426423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would they not exist in the Scandinavian region?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a problem with connecting them to local worship of any god. They are about sacred primal nature - not large motif I would see in Norse culture. And their sacred Prey - Hosts - are small threat in Scandinavia. Spiders are non-lethal, rats are few.<br /> <br /> Or maybe you have idea of connected Aesir god that could promote Hunters in Darkness way of thinking?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-03-2015, 07:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T04:41:43-08:00","id":426437,"title":"","content":"Isn't primal nature the schtick of the Vanir? They are the fertility and nature divinities. Also, maybe there are other Sharta messing up the gauntlet there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T04:46:53-08:00","id":426443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=426433#post426433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have a problem with connecting them to local worship of any god. They are about sacred primal nature - not large motif I would see in Norse culture. And their sacred Prey - Hosts - are small threat in Scandinavia. Spiders are non-lethal, rats are few.<br /> <br /> Or maybe you have idea of connected Aesir god that could promote Hunters in Darkness way of thinking?</div> </div> </div> </div>Whether or not they would be present won't be down to human community worship of gods akin to Black Wolf. It'll be down to the werewolves' own traditions based on their experiences with the Scandinavian worlds on each side of the Gauntlet. It'll be down to the presence of Hosts and other territory-befouling creatures that would inspire Uratha to call to Black Wolf for her patronage and aid in the hunt. It'll be down to whether the landscape, spiritually, physically and metaphorically, has sacred grounds and holy places that inspire devotion and honour from the Uratha such that some are driven to see protecting them as their foremost calling.<br /> <br /> As for Hosts, the 'natural' animals to which the Hosts are associated doesn't equate to whether the Hosts themselves are a significant threat or not. Local spider species being non-lethal doesn't mean that the Azlu in Scandinavia can't spit poison or just saw you in half with massive bone spurs. While the conditions that Beshilu tend to thrive under are probably uncommon in the region (not much in the way of densely packed concentrations of human settlement), I could see the Azlu thriving. They could have a fate-weaving slant to them, pitching them as monstrous and hungry seers that humans can sometimes convince to yield up knowledge, perhaps linked to Frigg. Who knows, go far north enough to where the population is even thinner, where there are few things to stop them, and perhaps colossal Azlu roam the frozen north, terrifying Hosts nearing the state of incarnating the Spinner Hag once more, against whom an entire pack might face their final showdown and go out in blood and glory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T05:35:06-08:00","id":426473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=426165#post426165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of main charms of <b>Werewolf</b> game, to me, is mixing local human culture with Uratha - without them, game loose many in my eyes. Saying do not need to mix Norse mythology with stories of Firstborns is great blow to my game experience - I count that developers in final chapter will try at least this.<br /> <br /> Looking more in to topic, we can not use Norse gods as other name for Firsborns - but still, some patrons worship is natural for Tribes members. Here are mine propositions what would be main patrons for Forsaken Tribes. There are not spiritual beings, only that most members would worship them most in day to day lives, as being part of their Norse culture.<br /> <br /> <b>Blood Talons</b> - Odin<br /> <b>Bone Shadows</b> - Odin, Freyja<br /> <b>Hunters in Darkness</b> - Here is big problem, maybe they do not exist in Norse Tribes?<br /> <b>Iron Masters</b> - Loki<br /> <b>Winter Wolf </b>- Thor<br /> <br /> Probably could be added at least one more to them in each - if you have ideas, write. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, I thought more about reasons for Uratha to raid churches in general - what about that their are looking for something? Like in local werewolves variant of Ragnarok there is Idigam that looks a lot like symbols used by Christianity and People want to stop them, partaking in raids?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> (First off, let me apologise in advance for any typos and weird spacing - writing on my tablet)<br /> <br /> I wholeheartedly agree with this idea: the gods were important and it makes sense that they'd be venerated alongside the Firstborn. I do disagree a little with how you've distributed the gods, so I'll throw out my own version of it, primary god marked in italics.<br /> <br /> <b>Blood Talons:</b> <i>Thor</i>, Tyr, Odin<br /> Reasoning: Thor is a god of strength, he is the foremost warrior in Asgard, and all around strong guy. Also a champion slayer of trolls and giants. Tyr, on the other hand (pun intended) is a great commander, and a war leader of the Aesir, and he gives bravery and strength to soldiers - an obvious patron for the more cerebral Talons. And then there is Odin. God of war, death, magic, wisdom and madness. Only the most brave and foolhardy Talons worship him, but none can stand up to their claws and teeth when the Rage take them.<br /> <br /> <b>Bone Shadows:</b> <i>Odin, Freyja,</i> Hel, Ran<br /> Reasoning: Odin and Freyja are complimentary gods, both are deities of magic, wisdom and death, and thus they earn veneration from the Hirfathra Hissu. Odin, while being associated with wolves, also is associated with madness, leaving many of the Shadows wary of him. Hel and Ran are also keepers of the dead, and thus worthy of veneration, Ran takes the souls of all those lost at sea, and Hel claims everyone who isn't taken by the others. Hel has a special place in the heart of the Bone Shadows, because they know that she is the final keeper of the dead; even the gods themselves will come to the realm of Hel Half-Dead in the end.<br /> <br /> <b>Hunters in Darkness:</b> <i>Ull</i>, Skadi, Nott, Heimdall<br /> Reasoning: Ull is both a great hunter, and a great warrior. Master of the wilds, and master of the foes, the choice to venerate Ull is obvious to the Meninna. Skadi was a jotunn who married in to the family of the Aesir, but she never lost her love for the mountains, she is prayed to by everyone who has to hear out far in winter time, and is thus an obvious choice for the Hunters. Nott is the goddess of the night, and the Hunters in Darkness see a kinship between her and themselves, which gives her a place in their rites. Heimdall, the watchman is also praised, as he is seen as the avatar of their oath to keep the sacred places safe.<br /> <br /> <b>Iron Masters: </b>Loki<br /> Reasoning: The Iron Masters keep their rites close to those of the human kin they hide among, and thus don't have special focus on any of the gods, they venerate them all. That said, the Masters' mindset of always cheating when they can has given a lot of them a special liking for the trickster god.<br /> <br /> <b>Storm Lords: </b>Thor, <i>Tyr, </i>Odin<br /> Reasoning: Tyr, the one-handed warrior-god is one of the foremost gods in the rites of the children of Winter Wolf. He is a brave and great commander, once the leader of the Aesir, who stepped down in favour of Odin, some say. He sacrificed his hand to chain Fenrir, but did not let that stop him from standing tall and mighty. Odin, likewise a great leader who gave up much, but wasn't weakened by his sacrifice, is worshipped by the Imnir, although with caution. The Lodge of Crows, and Lodge of Winter are said to favour him. Thor, god of strength and thunder seems like a perfect fit for the Lords, and indeed, he is venerated, especially by the members of the Lodge of Thunder,<br /> <br /> I am aware that my Iron Master part is very weak, but I couldn't find any way to give any other gods places of importance there. Which bothers me, because I would like to add Frigga and Frey somewhere...<br /> <br /> And once again, I don't see any particular spiritual reason for the sacking of churches and monasteries, it's just that they were easy pickings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T07:39:03-08:00","id":426568,"title":"","content":"There is a legend in one of the books about an idigam that lives within the moon and may one day awaken and destroy it. It wouldn't be inconceivable for werewolves to have a similar legend that might reference J\u00f6rmungandr. I guess with his connection to innovation and human society, it wouldn't be far fetched to imagine that before the moon-landing, there were some prophecies about Red Wolf's influence leading to the release of the fabled monsters of the moon, either.<br /> <br /> I don't know much about the Norse pantheon beyond the popular culture ones, but he might fit in place of a tinkerer or protector of man, or a questioner deity. Apparently he's seeking after a way to get the Uratha accepted among humanity, and is one of the more meddlesome of Firstborn when it comes to his tribe. A micro manager.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-03-2015, 11:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T08:24:59-08:00","id":426591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=426568#post426568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know much about the Norse pantheon beyond the popular culture ones, but he might fit in place of a tinkerer or protector of man, or a questioner deity. Apparently he's seeking after a way to get the Uratha accepted among humanity, and is one of the more meddlesome of Firstborn when it comes to his tribe. A micro manager.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are no gods of crafting, the Aesir and Vanir left all that to the Dwarfs/Svartalves, alas. When it comes to the protector of mankind we have Thor, and the meddlers are Odin and Loki. Both loved to walk among the mortals in disguise (Especially Odin) to test that people were moral and did what they should.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T18:36:24-07:00","id":464123,"title":"","content":"I read very interesting informations in the <b>Blasphemies</b>, about Mots - Norse-based Lodges, making loose alliance on cultural basis.<br /> <br /> Norse Uratha believes in <i>Lokgrim</i>, that is dark Firstborn of cunning and known from both aid and bedevil both Uratha and their enemies. What's interesting, is that he was concurrent to the Black Wolf as patron for Hunters in the Darkness. Am I only one seeing developers trying to have &quot;Loki Wolf&quot;, without letting go of Red Wolf for Iron Masters?<br /> <br /> There is talk about <i>Yggdrasil</i>, World Tree, that is Place-That-Isn't, stretching along the various realms, even various times. It is said to be scratched still by the claws of Father Wolf. Maybe it's the left of Border Marches, so discussed now in the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/388724-dark-eras-neolithic-chapter?p=460539#post460539\">Neolithic Chapter for Dark Eras</a>? And how, in now nWoD cosmology, would Nine Realms be connected by World Tree? Midgard is clearly the Material Plane, but others?<br /> <br /> The Mots themselves are shown two - <i>Valkyries</i> and <i>Eiwaz</i>. First are female Uratha that send dead to the All Father for the lst battle with idigam at the end of time - <b>and they believe All Father is Father Wolf! </b>With now Mother Wolf and Father Moon paradigm of 2ed I do not see this. Or we will have both &quot;Odin&quot; and &quot;<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/M%C3%A1ni\" target=\"_blank\">Mani</a>&quot; as creators of Uratha race, at least to the Norse werewolves. On one hand I would like to see setting with Two Fathers figures ( as non-heteronormative myself ), but even with two Fathers we could not have All Father then - when they are two Fathers, one of them could not be All Creator, yes? So how to resolve the Valkyries mythological problem here? Also, would not they send souls to the Underwold, in nWoD cosmology?<br /> <br /> Second Mot, <i>Eiwaz</i>, is basically <i>Get of Fenris</i> without calling them that way. They are brutal Uratha that fallows &quot;Noble Wolf&quot; and support hate groups, with philosophy of &quot;might makes right&quot;. They are even marked as probably the Pure agents in Forsaken society, with their strong similarities to Ivory Claws, even if Claws themselves are rejecting them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-31-2015, 09:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T19:24:01-07:00","id":464177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424265#post424265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For those mentioning the Abrahamic faiths: Islam very readily adjusts to the Hisil. The Djinn are a thing in their worldview, and their place beneath Allah is clearly defined.<br /> <br /> Christianity and Judaism are the ones more likely to have ... difficulties. And Bale Hounds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, depending on how closely one hews to the original conception of angels (wheels-within-wheels covered in eyes; layers of wings folded over a core of nothingness; that sort of thing), the argument can be made for at least some &quot;angels&quot; actually being spirits, never mind the spirit-tales of the host cultures (such as how some communities viewed 'fairies' as angels who remained neutral in the battle between God and Lucifer; banished from Heaven, but not necessarily evil <i>per se</i>).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T00:22:38-07:00","id":464384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=464123#post464123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I read very interesting informations in the <b>Blasphemies</b>, about Mots - Norse-based Lodges, making loose alliance on cultural basis.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope that when they dig into this, it'll be more faithful to the old faith than simply slapping Uratha-esque terms on everything, like taking Ragnar\u00f6k and keeping it intact, only putting in Idigam instead of giants. The old faith is a revived, and fairly active, religion, and this is an important part of the culture up here.<br /> I mean... to explain this. I saw you complain pretty noticeably about the spelling of polish names in Forsaken 2e. And that's something as simple as trying to cope with different alphabets.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=464123#post464123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Norse Uratha believes in <i>Lokgrim</i>, that is dark Firstborn of cunning and known from both aid and bedevil both Uratha and their enemies. What's interesting, is that he was concurrent to the Black Wolf as patron for Hunters in the Darkness. Am I only one seeing developers trying to have &quot;Loki Wolf&quot;, without letting go of Red Wolf for Iron Masters?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why do you conflate Lokgrim with Loki? To me he sounds more like the All-father, who also, conveniently is very well connected with wolves (and other scavengers), if he has to be any of the gods. Which I don't think is neccessary, I'll add.<br /> Besides, the mots aren't Norse Uratha. They are the descendants of Norse, Anglo-Saxon and other Germanic tribes. Not only based in their home-lands, but spread over the world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=464123#post464123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is talk about <i>Yggdrasil</i>, World Tree, that is Place-That-Isn't, stretching along the various realms, even various times. It is said to be scratched still by the claws of Father Wolf. Maybe it's the left of Border Marches, so discussed now in the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/388724-dark-eras-neolithic-chapter?p=460539#post460539\">Neolithic Chapter for Dark Eras</a>? And how, in now nWoD cosmology, would Nine Realms be connected by World Tree? Midgard is clearly the Material Plane, but others?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yggdrasil is pretty complicated to explain in Werewolf terms, but I immediately see two metaphors from Mage that could fit.<br /> The simple one is that it's a version of the Omphalos, the great astral border-stone that holds down reality.<br /> A more complicated one is that it is a metaphor for the Astral Path. It has roots in this reality, where three roots are planted, one in material, one in shadow, one in the underworld, and then it stretches upwards through the various realms. Not perfect, but not complicated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=464123#post464123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Mots themselves are shown two - <i>Valkyries</i> and <i>Eiwaz</i>. First are female Uratha that send dead to the All Father for the lst battle with idigam at the end of time - <b>and they believe All Father is Father Wolf! </b>With now Mother Wolf and Father Moon paradigm of 2ed I do not see this. Or we will have both &quot;Odin&quot; and &quot;<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/M%C3%A1ni\" target=\"_blank\">Mani</a>&quot; as creators of Uratha race, at least to the Norse werewolves. On one hand I would like to see setting with Two Fathers figures ( as non-heteronormative myself ), but even with two Fathers we could not have All Father then - when they are two Fathers, one of them could not be All Creator, yes? So how to resolve the Valkyries mythological problem here? Also, would not they send souls to the Underwold, in nWoD cosmology?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like the Valkyries, I really do. As an Uratha lodge they make sense. Although I'd play up the death-angle a lot more, and have them sworn to a deathlord of an underworld realm (or even better, one of two.).<br /> And I see no problem at all with One-Eye being female for a while, to create the Uratha. Loki transformed into a mare to seduce a Jotun's horse, and thus became the mother of Sleipnir, and the All-Father himself took up the study of magic. The latter part doesn't sound very feminine to us, but then it was. In fact, during the Lokasenna, One-Eye denounces Loki's manliness by pointing out that Loki acted as a mother to Sleipnir. Loki managed to win the argument though by replying with that thing about learning magic, which was even less manly.<br /> <br /> So, I see no problems with playing a bit with the genders, at least temporarily.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=464123#post464123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second Mot, <i>Eiwaz</i>, is basically <i>Get of Fenris</i> without calling them that way. They are brutal Uratha that fallows &quot;Noble Wolf&quot; and support hate groups, with philosophy of &quot;might makes right&quot;. They are even marked as probably the Pure agents in Forsaken society, with their strong similarities to Ivory Claws, even if Claws themselves are rejecting them.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Eiwas is a group of neo-nazis. No ifs, whens, or buts about it. They even have a fucking nazi symbol in their logo. They behave just like neo-nazis do, and they sprang up after WW2. They draw upon the same sources as the Get of Fenris, sure. But hey, so do Scandinavian Neo-nazis. The Eiwaz mot is all throughout their presentation shown to be creepy and monstrous, which I am fine with, but please, do not begin to normalize them by using them as a source of Norse-Uratha culture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T07:39:41-07:00","id":464659,"title":"","content":"It's been a while since I read that part of the book.<br /> <br /> I remember when I did read it, I thought they sort of hearkened back to the Greek hero or mystery cults, or maybe as a warrior culture, because it did seem to put an emphasis on being warriors.<br /> <br /> What would you say differentiates a mot from a lodge or tribe or protectorate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T15:17:18-07:00","id":465218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=464659#post464659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's been a while since I read that part of the book.<br /> <br /> I remember when I did read it, I thought they sort of hearkened back to the Greek hero or mystery cults, or maybe as a warrior culture, because it did seem to put an emphasis on being warriors.<br /> <br /> What would you say differentiates a mot from a lodge or tribe or protectorate?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they are very much Germanic-influenced. They sure are a warrior-culture, but the old Norse were very much a warrior culture, so it makes sense. Although I think the Valkyrja Mot plays up that part unnecessarily much, to the detriment of the other important parts of the valkyries, but I suppose that could be chalked up to them having existed for over a thousand years. There's bound to be some drift.<br /> <br /> And as far as I understand the examples, they are Lodges. Just another name for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T18:35:11-07:00","id":465439,"title":"","content":"Truth be told, the vikings weren't really a warrior culture so much as they were a trader and lawyer culture (seriously look up the viking legal code sometime, it's surprisingly progressive for it's time.) the raiding was just a small part of their culture. I get that warrior culture is what we want for forsaken, It's just that I am a huge history nerd who felt the need to say it. That being said, the viking court system didn't have public prosecutors and those who did proscute cases that they weren't personally involved in were doing it for wealth and fame. Which means that a viking Uratha might earn some renown by prosecuting a case well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T18:48:30-07:00","id":465449,"title":"","content":"I thought near the end they developed warrior cults.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T19:14:38-07:00","id":465472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=465439#post465439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Truth be told, the vikings weren't really a warrior culture so much as they were a trader and lawyer culture (seriously look up the viking legal code sometime, it's surprisingly progressive for it's time.) the raiding was just a small part of their culture. I get that warrior culture is what we want for forsaken, It's just that I am a huge history nerd who felt the need to say it. That being said, the viking court system didn't have public prosecutors and those who did proscute cases that they weren't personally involved in were doing it for wealth and fame. Which means that a viking Uratha might earn some renown by prosecuting a case well.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't mean they weren't also a warrior culture. I mean, you just need to look at their gods to see that. The All-father, Thor, Freyja, Tyr, Ull and probably a bunch I forget, are all war gods. Or at the very least, warrior gods.<br /> And look at the fates of the dead, those who die in battle are taken either to Sessrumnir or Valhalla to war and feast until the end of days. People who drown at sea are taken to Ran's halls (which may or may not be a nice place), and those who died for other reasons were doomed to stand in a river of poison until the end of days.<br /> <br /> I'm not arguing that the old Norse weren't also very well developed in other ways. Hell, I'll be one of the first to claim that they WERE well-developed, but at their core they were a warrior culture.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T19:17:11-07:00","id":465477,"title":"","content":"(Sorry for double-posting, using a tablet..)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=465449#post465449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought near the end they developed warrior cults.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if you talk about the Jomsvikings, then they weren't exactly a warrior cult, but rather very traditionalistic mercenaries, that stuck to the old gods. It's also not certain if they were, actually, real.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T23:24:24-07:00","id":602609,"title":"","content":"A little topic necromancy, as I got idea on it...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=424093#post424093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Hati is Silver Wolf, what would that make Skoll?</div> </div> </div> </div>If Hati is Silver Wolf, maybe Skoll is other Pure Totem? I say that the Rabid Wolf of Fire-Touched could have sense here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T13:22:47-07:00","id":603159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=602609#post602609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A little topic necromancy, as I got idea on it...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If Hati is Silver Wolf, maybe Skoll is other Pure Totem? I say that the Rabid Wolf of Fire-Touched could have sense here.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That... Actually makes sense.<br /> I mean, his name means traitor or treachery. Which fits Rabid Wolf's difficulty in choosing side between the Pure and the Forsaken.<br /> He is a beast of the apocalypse, which will appeal to the eschatological among the Fire Touched.<br /> Sun = Fire. Duh.<br /> Sk\u00f6ll is fated to eat the sun, and in WoD terms, that'd stop the tyranny of the sun over the spirits, whom he keep suppressed. Something the Fire Touched would very much like.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T23:06:20-07:00","id":606375,"title":"","content":"On the other hand, there doesn't seem to be any evidence that Helios and Luna get along at all, so Skoll eating the sun could be from devotion to Luna, as another option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T02:37:46-07:00","id":606439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/424015-if-you-would-done-vikings-werewolf?p=606375#post606375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> On the other hand, there doesn't seem to be any evidence that Helios and Luna get along at all, so Skoll eating the sun could be from devotion to Luna, as another option.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno. Helios is still pissed that the werewolves killed his brother-in-law. So either Helios got along well with the Wolf (which would mean Sk\u00f6ll breaks that tradition), or he really likes his sister, and was a brother of the &quot;You bother my sister, and I kick your teeth out&quot; school of siblings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T02:48:17-07:00","id":606444,"title":"","content":"Viking Forsaken, uhm.<br /> <br /> As I am a germanic/viking reenactor I'll try to say something about it.<br /> First of all I will keep the chronicle very dark, darker than the modern nWod, I'm scared by the idea that the whole forsaken chronicle can become a low-budget fantasy crap. High Medieval age don't help too much. By the way. Everyone says something about religion, but I want to say something about the setting with some chronicle ideas.<br /> My ideas about High medieval chronicles setted in northern Europe:<br /> <br /> <b>- Wolf Blooded and </b><b>\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0na</b>r, a group of blood talons wolf blooded is approached by a Jarl who offer them the role of ''elite'' warriors to protect him against another ruler who wants his lands, he want's to scare the shit out of him with the idea of wolf-headed warriors. Berserkers was used for this type of tasks, and they were a really rare type of warrior among the scandinavian society.<br /> What will happen if the blood talons discover it? What if the Jarl has some secrets?<br /> <b>-Christianity spread among the norsemen</b>, Denmark, 950 ac. Churces are build across the country. People are starting pray the White Christ. The forsaken packs are for the most spiritual/pagan, they grow with legends about Wotan and Thor and some of them <i>saw and talked</i> with the Gods (powerful spirits). But, somewhere, a pack of Fired Touched see the advantage of the new religion: no lies, grow the herd and lead the sheeps. And burn those who do not want understand the true words of the White Christ. Destroy the ancient idols, Skolis, Hati, Garmr, Fenris, they are all fathers and mothers of the forsaken traitors. What will do the troupe if a very powerful izidak use the christian-human population to hunt down the pagan-tainted berserkers ?<br /> <b>-The other face of the coin</b>, if the troupe want to play an urban-pack. A lot of people who lives in the town are at least christians. A lot of wolf blooded too. People around the city start killing more wolves and bears every days, the bible is very clear: the wolves are the spawn of Satan, from hell to kill and eat the herd of God. But the Predator Kings are not very excited about it.<br /> The pure starts to kill and dismember as much people as they can, during the night they run across the border of the city hunting down humans and wolf blooded alike. Keep the chronicle horror. Not gauru form dancing on a tons of bodies in the center of the city. They took one or 2 humans every week. They are not stupid, they know about the dangers from humanity. Fired Touched and Ivory claws try to replace the new god with the ancient one-eyed god from the city. But what about the forsaken tribes who support polytheism?<br /> <b>-All War across the Storm, </b>the pack is composed by Suthar Anzuth and Iminir. And they gladly left Scandinavia in search of a new territory in England. Arrived in England they join the great Heathen army under the command of Ivarr and Halfdan, sons of Ragnarr Lothbrok. But once they arrive in London, to siege it, they realized that their armony is becoming to high, too much life among soldiers and human things. It's time to find a territory and hold it with fangs and claws. Nice idea to understand the new rules about harmony and understand the difference between the human and uratha existence.<br /> <b>-Ancient Nightmares, </b>Hordaland, Norway. A pack of bone shadows vanish in the northern part of the region. Only one is alive but he's diyng. He tell something about a mountain, and an ancient horror living on his roots. During the next week a lot of wolf blooded and uratha are tortured by nightmares and they lost essence during this process, but the pack seems to be immune. Packs near the troupe territory start to think that the fault about all of this fall to the troupe pack. They have to discover the truth and find a solution. Patrolling the mountain could be a good Idea, they will find a comunity of seidrmen (norse shamans and runemaster) who wait for their master. They are mages worshipping and ancient Nightmarespirit who gives them astral and dreaming power. Now he is awake. Soon , also the human population fo Bergen will dream about horrors and other terrible things, and start talking about the Mara, and other norse demons.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Religion is not a problem to me</b>.<br /> Basically, the truth about Luna and Urfarah is darker than the 1st edition. So let every tribe, every pack, to have teir own theory.<br /> Hati could be Silver Wolf as much as Urfarah (mother wolf) following the Moon (father moon).<br /> Maybe could be mother wolf for some uratha and silver wolf for some Pure.<br /> Fenris could be for sure the totem of the Blood Talons, but maybe the traditional history of the tribes says that it's not true that he's son fo Loki. They are Warriors and they Respect Odin for sure.<br /> Skoll could be Winter wolf, he wants to scare the Sun to make sure that their children become stronger with long and dangerous winters, but could be Rabid wolf who wants the favor of Elios to destroy the moon-lovers.<br /> There are, really, infinite options.<br /> Religion is also one of the main focus of Forsaken, options are not a problems.<br /> <br /> <br /> sorry fo my very rusty english.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}